**Chapter 10, Section 1: 'Friends'**

"You're telling me she was acting just like herself, that damn Princess. Going right on being self-absorbed to the very end."

As Felt said this, taking a sip from her teacup, Emilia lowered the corners of her eyes.

Seated directly opposite her on a reception sofa, hugging one knee, Felt had listened to Emilia's story without interruption and now mourned Priscilla in her own characteristic way.

Emilia didn't think it heartless that no deep sorrow or sense of loss passed through Felt's eyes, which held a slightly different shade of red than Priscilla's. She simply thought Felt was strong. That included the fact that Felt had taken the initiative to come here to learn the details of Priscilla's death.

Right now, Emilia and Felt were facing each other in a room within the royal mansions of the Royal Capital of Lugunica. It was the reception room of one of the mansions reserved for important figures staying in the capital, where Emilia was hosting Felt.

They hadn't arranged it. Felt, who happened to be staying in the capital, had heard that Emilia had come to the royal castle with a report, and had come to see her like this.

Honestly, Emilia was very happy that Felt had come to visit like this.

To begin with, the Emilia camp owed Felt a significant debt—Annerose had told her that Meili had been looked after tremendously while they were away from the kingdom.

They had asked Annerose, a relative of Roswaal and a supporter of Emilia, to handle various negotiations concerning Meili and the Pleiades Watchtower. Apparently, Felt and her group had greatly assisted in making those negotiations succeed.

Because of that too, Emilia had intended to make time to go and thank Felt herself, so meeting like this was a great help.

Though, if only she could have brought back a better story while she was at it—

"Lookin' like you're thinkin' something like that, Sister Emilia."
"Huh? Was I making a face that obvious?"
"Pretty damn much. Scowling with your head down like that, it's a dead giveaway."

Tapping her own forehead with her finger, Felt prompted Emilia to rub her own brow with her finger as well.

She was often told that her thoughts showed easily on her face, but to be so specific about it was surprising even to herself. And it also made her uneasy. —She had been holding herself together, thinking 'I've completely recovered now, I'm fine. Everyone, you don't need to worry,' trying to keep up her spirits.

"And yet, no good. If I'm like this, Subaru and the others will get mad at me."
"Bro over there gettin' all prickly with you, Sister Emilia? Can't really imagine that."
"That's not true. Subaru also needs me to be dependable. So, he tells me properly about my bad points."
"Huh~, really now?"

Laughing like that, Felt rested her chin on her raised knee, letting her double canine teeth peek out.

Pursing her lips at Felt's somewhat mean, teasing smile, Emilia said "But," and continued,
"It seems my thoughts were completely visible to you, Felt-chan... but don't you feel the same way?"
"It's a bit complicated, but you mean, like, even though it's been a while since we last met face to face like this, it's a shame the topic ended up being the Princess's death report?"
"Umm, yes... that's right. Yeah, that's what I mean."
"In that case, I'm actually glad I heard it from you, Sister Emilia."
"Glad you heard it from me?"

Surprised by the unexpected statement, Emilia repeated the question back, and Felt nodded with an "Ah." While Emilia watched wide-eyed, Felt scratched her head.

"Honestly, when I heard that Princess had died, I thought it was a joke. She was like the poster girl for women you couldn't kill even if you tried. Left as is, in my head, all sorts of random imaginings would've just swelled up, and the real facts would've gotten buried."
"————"
"So, being able to hear it from you, Sister Emilia, who was actually there, for me, it's... settled things. ...Nah, more like it's prepared me to settle things. Tch, I ended up with a complicated way of saying it too. Sorry."
"—. No, I think I understand what you mean, Felt-chan."

Felt made a sour face, unable to explain well, but her feelings got through to Emilia.

If their positions were reversed, if Emilia heard somewhere far away that someone she knew had died without her knowing, she too would imagine all sorts of things surrounding that death.

Her head would fill with all those imaginings, things that might be right or wrong, things impossible to verify, and she wouldn't know the truth anymore.

So, even if it's very painful, having someone cut off that room for speculation is a relief.

"And if the person telling you is someone you trust, I think it's even better."
"...Doesn't that mean I'm saying I trust you, Sister Emilia?"
"Yes, I trust you too, Felt-chan... and you feel the same, right? That's why you came to see me like this, isn't it?"
"Technically, we're rival candidates, so it'd be weird for me to nod to that here!"

Taking her feet down from the chair, Felt rested her cheek on her hand with a exasperated look. But since Felt didn't shake her head 'no,' Emilia smiled with a feeling of relief.

Thinking of Priscilla, Emilia's chest still ached with a dull pain. But she was glad that she could keep Felt's tangled feelings from being left buried as they were.

"————"

Then, a faint breath cut into their exchange. Immediately, Felt, with her sharp ears, caught it and made an irritated sound, "Hey."

"You, what're you grinning at?"
"—No, my apologies. It's just that seeing Lady Felt being so directly countered by Lady Emilia is quite a rare sight, I couldn't help myself."
"Couldn't help yourself, my ass. What kind of knight just smirks while watching his master get told off?"
"Forgive me. I hesitated to interrupt your conversation."

Saying that, the person who placed a hand on his chest and bowed was Felt's knight, distinguished by his red hair and blue eyes—Reinhard.

Naturally, there was no way Felt would visit Emilia alone; he too had been listening to the conversation until now. Seeing Reinhard and Felt's friendly banter, Emilia began with a "Honestly," and said,

"You didn't have to be so considerate. Even my Otto-kun has been part of the conversation from the start... Huh? He wasn't in here?"
"That's right. Thank you for noticing. Even I have the discretion not to interrupt a conversation between two such esteemed persons, you know. Actually."

Next to Emilia, who raised her eyebrows in surprise, Otto smiled wryly. He had been there the whole time.

This time, only Otto had accompanied Emilia to the capital, so naturally, he accompanied her everywhere—for the report to the royal castle and for meetings at the royal mansions. Otto's very presence brought a sense of security, so Emilia had grown completely accustomed to his silence.

"Sorry, I didn't notice. Since Otto-kun likes to talk so much, staying quiet must have been really hard for him."
"Let me say, I only talk when necessary in necessary situations, I shouldn't be categorized as someone who particularly 'likes to talk,' you know!"
"Oh, oh, what a load of crap with zero persuasiveness. You're telling me a guy who can chat not just with people, but with bugs and land dragons, doesn't like to talk?"
"I'd appreciate it if you didn't lump my Divine Protection talk with my personality."

Pressing down on the green hat on his head, Otto responded to Felt's familiar tone.

Given Otto's ability to talk to various living things with his 'Divine Protection of Soul Language,' Emilia felt Felt's point was spot-on. Come to think of it, wherever they went, it was Otto who would talk to animals, insects, and all sorts of creatures, expanding his circle of friends.

"Otto-kun has so-o many friends. I don't have many friends, so I really respect how he can get along with anyone."
"It's a bit different when you call them 'friends.' Often, what I initiate with others are negotiations or deals, which require different know-how from making friends. Thinking that way, I probably can't say I have many friends either."
"No point gettin' all hung up on the definition of a friend. If anything, why don't you become friends with our Reinhard here? This guy's also someone with few friends."
"Eh, really? That's so-o surprising."

In response to Felt's words, pointing at Reinhard standing behind the sofa with one eye closed, Emilia couldn't help but look up at the red-haired knight.

Reinhard was amiable, very famous, surely known by name and relied upon by anyone in the kingdom. Emilia herself had been treated kindly by him ever since their first meeting, so she had almost thought he was friends with everyone in the kingdom.

Under Emilia's surprised gaze, Reinhard continued, "Unfortunately,"

"Leaving aside my side of things, it seems I often make the other party shrink back. Even within the knight order or comrades from the camp... excluding Subaru and Ferris, I may not have many friends."
"Is that so. Even Reinhard has worries like that... Hey, Otto-kun, if it's okay, could you become friends with Reinhard for me?"
"That's a terribly outrageous request, but wouldn't that be insulting from Sir Reinhard's perspective!?"
"Not outrageous at all. In fact, I'd welcome it greatly. Will you be my friend?"
"Isn't this a pincer attack, or rather, an ambush?"

Sandwiched between Emilia's gaze and Reinhard's smile, Otto groaned, "Guhngh."

Only Felt watched this with a grin, but after agonizing for a while, Otto let out a big, deep sigh.

"As Lady Felt mentioned earlier, right now, we are members of opposing camps. Until the Royal Selection is over, we should avoid becoming overly familiar."
"I see. That's a shame, but if that is your wish, I will respect it. Even if we aren't friends."
"Yes, please do that. We are not friends, after all."

Otto, who said this lonely thing while his shoulders slumped, and Reinhard, who oddly enough didn't seem hurt or disappointed but smiled through the exchange. Unfortunately, they couldn't become friends, but to Emilia's eyes, they somehow seemed to have an atmosphere like friends.

And moreover—

"My, my, the tea has gone completely cold. I'll brew a fresh pot. Please continue your pleasant conversation, Lady Emilia. As for me—"
"—. In that case, I'll join you. Even if we couldn't become friends, let me show you the effects of the 'Divine Protection of Tea Ceremony.'"
"It seems you hold a grudge surprisingly easily, and being held a grudge by the 'Sword Saint' makes life feel unbearable."

Somehow, chatting like that, the two of them left the room together.

Watching Otto and the others' backs, cut off by the closing door, Emilia turned back to Felt.

"Somehow, it really seemed like they were friends, didn't it?"
"Kuku, yeah, I thought so too. Usually, I'm just pissed off at that guy Reinhard's attitude, but when it's about other people, it's super funny to watch."
"Ah, such a mischievous face. But, because of our Royal Selection situation, making Otto-kun hold back on becoming friends with Reinhard..."
"Pfft, that's just that guy using my words as a convenient excuse. I can't even see why he'd do that... 'We can't get along because of the Royal Selection,' who'd take that seriously?"
"It's okay... not to take it seriously?"

Felt's attitude was so triumphant, she seemed about to hum a tune. After thinking for a bit, Emilia said "Alright," and stood up.

Otto, thinking of the Royal Selection, had given up on becoming friends with Reinhard. She felt sorry for Otto's decision and consideration, but Emilia had decided.

Because of what happened with Priscilla, she didn't want to have any more regrets.

"Hey, Felt-chan, is it okay?"
"Huh? What's up?"

Walking over briskly, Emilia lowered herself next to Felt, who looked up at her, facing her directly at a distance where their shoulders almost touched. Emilia's momentum made Felt, who had been approached so closely, blink her red eyes.

Thinking about it now, Emilia and Felt first met when Emilia had her Royal Selection participant qualification stolen by her. Back then, Emilia's mind went blank, and she even felt like taking it out on Puck for not panicking in that situation, but in any case, their meeting was definitely not a good start.

Even so, right now, Emilia felt this towards Felt, her fellow Royal Selection candidate.

"I want to become good friends with you, Felt-chan. And not just good friends, but really, really close best friends."
"...Huh?"

To Felt, who swayed her large eyes in confusion, Emilia pressed on clearly.

"Actually, I made a promise with Anastasia-san that we'd become friends after the Royal Selection is over. Traveling together and talking about all sorts of things... It wasn't all really Anastasia-san, but we talked a lot, and then we made that promise."

The promise she made with Anastasia—since Anastasia strongly identified as a merchant, she would surely keep it. Unlike Subaru, making a promise with her felt safe.

"Subaru breaks promises right away so it's worrying, but with Anastasia-san, it's safe. But, regardless of promises, I don't think I could become friends with Subaru, and I don't even feel like I want to become friends with Subaru... Huh? What was I talking about?"
"You were saying you couldn't become friends with Subaru-bro?"
"Yes, that's right... That's not it, it's about me and you, Felt-chan!"

With a feeling of relief that she had nearly lost the main topic, Emilia felt a chill. Right in front of Emilia, who had narrowly avoided that, Felt suddenly looked up. Following her movement, Emilia also looked at the ceiling. She couldn't see anything in particular.

"Felt-chan?"
"Not lookin' at the ceiling. Just thinkin', what should I do~"
"Um, right. Subaru and Petra-chan often tell me that looking at my face makes them feel really energized. How about it?"
"Are you maybe trying to tell me your good points?"
"Yes, because I want to be friends with you, Felt-chan."

After this past year and a bit, even Emilia had grown accustomed to looking at her own face in the mirror.

Since Subaru and Petra, and occasionally Ram too, praised Emilia's face, she thought maybe it would work on Felt too, and gave it a shot.

To Emilia's determined approach, Felt, still with her face tilted upward, said,

"Why d'you wanna be friends with me so bad? It's not like things as they are now are..."
"I wanted... to be friends with Priscilla."
"————"
"But I kept putting off telling her that. I'm no good, aren't I? Even though I should have known that a sudden farewell could come even with someone important who was fine until yesterday."

Clutching her chest tightly, touching the magic crystal hanging from her neck, Emilia murmured.

It was the same with Puck, who continues to sleep, and with Emilia's precious family frozen in ice in the Elior Forest. Farewells come suddenly, even to those who matter most.

Priscilla's farewell had reminded forgetful Emilia of that sad fact.

"I don't want to forget that again. So I decided not to hold back anymore. To tell the people I like that I like them, and to tell the people I want to be friends with that I want to be friends."
"—Damn it, that Princess really went and did it right to the very end."
"—?"

Emilia had put her feelings into words as honestly as possible. Felt, who had been listening while still looking up, slowly lowered her gaze.

Felt's expression was a smile, different from a frustrated or bitter one.

"Fine, I get it. I'll be friends with you too, Sister Emilia."
"Really!? You mean, after the Royal Selection is over..."
"Nah, that's fine. If it's gonna happen anyway, I'll become friends with you before Anastasia-sis and make her jealous."
"Ah, don't say that. Anastasia-san is going to be my friend too."
"Wouldn't I, who's already your friend, rank higher than Anastasia-sis, who's not your friend yet, in Sister Emilia's mind?"
"Stop teasing me!"

Emilia couldn't help but let her lips relax into a smile at Felt, who laughed, showing her double canines.

Felt had given a happy response to her proposal. With the feeling of actually becoming friends with Felt, Emilia's chest slowly filled with warmth.

Laughing together with Felt like that, Emilia thought. —About Al, who still couldn't fully accept Priscilla's death, and Subaru and the others who were accompanying him.

"With Al, too—"

Someday. It didn't have to be right now, but someday.

She wanted to sincerely pray for the day to come when she could talk about Priscilla, whom she wished to be friends with, with an expression other than tears.

Yes, Emilia thought this while leaning close to her friend.

△▼△▼△▼△

"—So, you even signaled with your eyes. You have something to talk about with me, right?"

Having left just Emilia and Felt in the reception room, Reinhard brought this up after they had walked down the corridor for a while.

Carrying a silver tray with the tea set, Otto nodded without turning around, "Indeed."

"It helps that you sensed it. Lady Felt came to visit, and Lady Emilia finally seemed to laugh naturally again, so I didn't want to ruin that atmosphere."
"As I thought, she was really holding back about Lady Priscilla."
"Honestly, anyone who participated in that battle was holding back. Even I, who had almost no connection to her, feel a sense of futility."

Of course, the shock Otto received was nothing compared to Emilia, who had felt goodwill toward Priscilla, or Subaru and Al, who witnessed her disappear before their eyes.

Even so, for Otto, who had intended to act to ensure as many allies as possible survived the battle against the 'Great Disaster,' the death of a person related to the kingdom—a Royal Selection candidate—had hit quite hard. On the other hand, there was also a part of him that coolly analyzed the departure of a rival candidate with absurd charisma.

"...That's unexpected."

As if hearing that inner voice of Otto's, Reinhard murmured that. Glancing back at him from the corner of his eye, Reinhard indeed looked surprised, his eyebrows raised.

Responding to that reaction, Otto relaxed the corner of his mouth with a slightly self-mocking air,

"Was that reaction because you were surprised I was pained by Lady Priscilla's death? Certainly, it would be a lie to say I had no feelings of welcoming the departure of a rival candidate..."
"No, I was surprised that you honestly voiced your own weakness. You don't have to deliberately create such a pseudo-villainous version of yourself, you know?"
"————"
"Or is revealing your true feelings a sign of letting your guard down... a sign we could become friends?"
"It seems I chose my words poorly."

Teased jokingly, Otto lifted his shoulders a bit in annoyance and resumed walking.

Somehow, it seemed his mental state was worse than he himself realized. Having understood that, Reinhard likely let his recent blunder slide as just a moment of banter.

"Get a grip, Otto Suwen."

He tightened his own reins, thinking this wouldn't do.

No matter how much Felt held no hostility towards Emilia, they were still rival candidates. It was best not to show weakness to the other side. Showing a state of mental imbalance was probably one of the worst postures he could display.

Conscious of that once more, Otto carried out the purpose for which he had drawn Reinhard out.

That was—

"—Let's share information about Heinkel Astrea."
"————"

He could clearly sense the air in the corridor change at the raised topic.

Did it dry or moisten? The humidity changed. Did it rise or fall? The temperature changed. And the only certainty was that it was caused by the 'Sword Saint' walking right beside him.

"About Heinkel-san... He participated in the battle in the empire as a member of Lady Priscilla's camp and survived. However, after Lady Priscilla's death, he was witnessed being terribly distraught, and then his whereabouts became unknown..."
"...Was he captured and held by the empire?"
"No, I doubt that. While it's a country capable of becoming utterly ruthless for the sake of profit, having been exhausted in that battle, they are not people so blind to the situation as to make an enemy of the kingdom—of the 'Sword Saint' Reinhard van Astrea."
"Then, he voluntarily went into hiding, is that it?"

Reinhard lowered his eyes slightly and muttered weakly, which Otto heard.

He hadn't intended it as retaliation, but it ended up creating a situation where the other party's mental balance was lacking, just like Otto's earlier blunder. However, he wasn't in the mood to take advantage and pry into or explore the other's weakness now.

Honestly, he thought he was unsuited for it, but—

"Heinkel-san... your father, are you worried about him?"

Asking that of the other was genuine concern for the one who had shown him consideration.

In reality, it was probably a difficult question for Reinhard. Otto didn't know the details of the relationship between Reinhard and Heinkel, but the fact that this parent-child relationship was cracked and broken was already common knowledge.

Moreover, Otto had even encountered the scene in Priestella where Heinkel pointed his sword at Felt and tried to restrain Reinhard's movements.

If you were to say that, the very situation where all three generations of the family supported different Royal Selection candidates boldly spoke of the Astrea family's dysfunction.

In any case—

"Whether it's a consolation or not, according to Garfiel, your father was said to have even withstood a blow from the 'Dragon.' So, I think the possibility of him being attacked and in mortal danger is low."

While conveying this, Otto intentionally omitted the possibility of Heinkel taking his own life.

From what he heard, Heinkel, distraught over Priscilla's death, was so desperate that he asked Emilia to switch his loyalty to her and begged to be taken under her wing. Having been refused by Emilia, it couldn't be said with absolute certainty that he, with nowhere to go, might not be driven to extremes—

"—That won't happen, Otto. Father would never choose to end his own life."
"...Was I as easy to read as Lady Emilia?"

Having his inner thoughts precisely hit, Otto rubbed his forehead with one hand. Reinhard then showed a bitter smile and said, "No,"

"You deliberately avoided mentioning the worst possibility, so I thought you were being considerate. But that worry is unfounded. Father has a purpose he absolutely must live to accomplish. Choosing death without fulfilling that is unthinkable for him."
"If that's the case, while it's reassuring, it also increases anxiety. I wonder what he'll do, driven into a corner... Perhaps he'll make contact with Lady Felt next?"

For Heinkel, it would be a much more viable option than clinging to Emilia.

Of course, that choice would negate Heinkel's one and only absolute advantage—the ability to exert some kind of coercive power over the 'Sword Saint' Reinhard. But even setting that aside, it was a choice with a high probability of being taken in.

Having lost Priscilla and been rejected by Emilia, Otto considered it a sufficiently plausible choice for Heinkel to choose Felt as his next host.

However—

"—That's also unlikely."

That was said with even more certainty than before, cutting off Otto's next words.

"————"

Into those blue eyes that reflected a clear sky, a shadowy hue, like a night covering them, mixed in. Even the trace of a smile at his mouth vanished as Reinhard walked beside the silenced Otto.

Two steps, three steps, they closed the distance to the kitchen without a word. It seemed the conversation would end in silence, but then,

"Father wants to make me quit being the 'Sword Saint.' So, it's unthinkable that he would lend his strength to Lady Felt, whom I support, in a Royal Selection where I absolutely must not lose."
"...He wants to win the Royal Selection. But you don't want him to win?"
"That's right. On that single point, Father and I are incompatible. No matter what Father wishes, I am the 'Sword Saint.' —I have to be the 'Sword Saint.'"

Everyone has their own circumstances, he supposed.

That much he understood well, so Otto had no intention of poking his nose into another family's affairs. Even if he felt it was undoubtedly a distorted relationship between parent and child, and even if that last line sounded like Reinhard telling it to himself.

Therefore, all Otto could do was clarify his own stance.

"—. My, my, that was quite an extraordinary scene. I never thought in my life I'd have a casual chat like this with the 'Sword Saint.'"

Shrugging his shoulders like that, Otto showed Reinhard a stance of not delving into personal matters.

It was a survival skill he'd honed as a traveling merchant, meeting various people in different positions across many lands. No matter what circumstances he heard, he would overtly show he wouldn't exploit them, declaring himself harmless.

In most cases, that allowed him to leave town without incident.

"Sometimes there are unreasonable people who, carried away by drink, spill information they absolutely mustn't, and then try to silence the person who heard it..."

So, even in taverns, the best places to gather information while traveling, one needed to take care not to inadvertently obtain overly critical information. Such lessons from being a traveling merchant had, as it turned out, proven useful even while being involved in the Royal Selection—talk about life being unpredictable.

In any case—

"Thank you for sharing about my father. I'll keep it in mind."

Reinhard also nodded as if accepting Otto's declaration of intent. Accepting that, Otto also shrugged and continued, "Sorry about that."

"Did I just add to your unnecessary worries? In your position as the 'Sword Saint,' you must already have plenty of things to trouble over."
"It's a Divine Protection and position I wished for. I suppose that's my responsibility."

Divine Protections are bestowed things.

He thought it an odd way to put it, saying he 'wished for it,' but Otto quickly remembered that the 'Sword Saint's Divine Protection' was an exception—something inherited by a worthy successor after the previous holder's death.

Reinhard too was in that position, having inherited it after the death of the previous 'Sword Saint.'

"For a Divine Protection holder, the troubles of dealing with one's own Divine Protection are endless. From what I've seen, Otto, you seem to have mastered yours quite well, so perhaps it's not like that for you?"
"Mastered it, that's ridiculous. I've been at the mercy of this uncontrollable Divine Protection since birth. If I could give it to someone, I'd gladly hand it over."
"Haha, you shouldn't say careless things. There are many who envy those with Divine Protections. Of course, I think I don't need to tell you that."
"I honestly don't think it's anything enviable."

As Reinhard said, for Divine Protection holders, the troubles with their Divine Protections are endless.

It's like continually answering difficult questions with no model answer, something that cannot be shared not only with those without Divine Protections but even among those with different Divine Protections.

Otto's reply to Reinhard's pleasantry was also undoubtedly his true feeling. —He had never once been so conceited as to think he had 'mastered' the 'Divine Protection of Soul Language.' Probably never would.

"It's not like yours, Sir Reinhard's 'Sword Saint's Divine Protection,' something that leaves a name in history."
"I wish you wouldn't put so much emphasis on 'Sword Saint,' 'Sword Saint.' After all, I'm still in an immature position being swayed by the title. I have no intention of acting high and mighty because of it."
"They say the position makes the person. Even if you're not aware of it, you might be intimidating those around you with that 'Sword Saint'-like quality, Sir Reinhard."
"'Sword Saint'-like quality intimidation... Could I hear more about that? Maybe that's the reason I get told all sorts of things by Lady Felt and Ratrius and the others."
"I'm in trouble if you take a casual remark and run with it!"

Unexpectedly seized upon, Otto let out a cry of distress under Reinhard's barrage of questions.

Transitioning into a somewhat lighter, thinner exchange, Otto slightly lowered his guard towards Reinhard and created a little room and leeway in his mind.

At the very least now, Otto had no reason to rush into political maneuvering at the cost of lowering his standing with Felt or Reinhard. His own condition wasn't good either.

More than anything, right about now, in a distant land, Subaru was in the midst of agonizing over Al.

"Even I feel guilty about scheming behind the scenes while Natsuki-san and the others are trying to save someone's heart. —Unlike the Margrave Mathers, that is."

Unlike Subaru and the others who headed for the Pleiades Watchtower with Al, Roswaal, who took along Shult, Priscilla's attendant, and accompanied him to her territory, the Barriere Domain. There was no doubt that behind his concern and consideration lay the aim to interfere with the Barriere Domain, seizing this opportunity.

That action was correct and zealous as a Royal Selection participant, and worthy of contempt. —At the same time, it made him feel both that he himself, who couldn't be that ruthless, was naive, and also that he was better off.

"Well then, shall we brew the tea? Allow me to show my skills."
"Don't hold back. I'll be watching your technique."

As soon as they reached the kitchen, Reinhard took the tea set from the silver tray and began preparations. Watching this, Otto let out a breath for a moment's rest, along with considering future developments.

But he had a premonition. A premonition that something would move again soon.

"...They're postponing Lady Emilia and Lady Felt's entry to the castle, prioritizing some discussion at the castle. I wonder what's going on."

As Otto murmured this, a small shadow lurking in the shadows of a pillar beside him stirred. —It was the Zolda insect he had struck a deal with to report if there was any movement at the castle.

—Otto's premonition would prove correct in two ways.

One was the report from the Zolda insect that the discussion at the castle, which deliberately excluded the Royal Selection candidates, had reached some conclusion.

The other was a report from the girl from Felt's camp who visited the royal mansion—Grasis.

It was the tumultuous report of trouble arising on the side of Subaru and the others who headed for the Pleiades Watchtower, resulting in Al being taken into custody, and Subaru and the others heading for the Royal Capital.
